    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102840": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice - Biology",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor of Practice - Biology Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Practice - Biology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the Faculty Academic/Administrative Information form. Attach the following documents: A cover letter highlighting the candidate’s interests and qualifications Curriculum Vitae A three-page teaching statement (Uploaded as \"Other Document\" The names and contact information for three references The teaching statement should summarize instructional experiences related to the position, teaching philosophy, and instructional methods as well as strategies for supporting students of all backgrounds. Although this is a teaching focused position, the successful candidate is expected to maintain research and/or scholarly activity. The teaching statement should therefore include a paragraph about how your research interests, background, and plans complement your teaching interests. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant Professor of Practice - Biology Department School of Biological Sciences-1076 Requisition Number F_260122 Posting Open Date 10/15/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 12/01/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled No Description of Work The School of Biological Sciences ( SBS ) in the College of Arts and Sciences ( CAS ) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Practice in Biology. This position will be primarily responsible for teaching Human Anatomy Lecture and the Human Anatomy Laboratory. The successful candidate will provide critical instruction and expertise in human gross anatomy courses taken by pre-health science majors and others across the university. They will teach high-enrollment Human Anatomy courses, coordinate the accompanying lab course with multiple sections, and teach an additional biology course within their disciplinary area. Candidates who have an ability to teach and mentor students of all backgrounds are highly encouraged to apply. They will contribute to the university’s mission to promote excellence through dedicated teaching, ongoing scholarly activity, and professional service. This is a teaching-focused, promotable, non-tenure track position with a renewable multi-year contract. SBS offers a collaborative, interdisciplinary, and welcoming environment (learn more at https://biosci.unl.edu ), and UNL maintains an active community of discipline-based educational researchers across STEM disciplines. The city of Lincoln, Nebraska provides an outstanding quality of life that includes a vibrant downtown, a lively music and art scene, over 120 parks, 130 miles of trails, and a low cost of living (learn more at https://aboutlincoln.unl.edu/ . Minimum Required Qualifications A terminal degree (PhD, MD, DO, DDS , DPT , DC or equivalent) in biology, biology education, or a related discipline is required by time of appointment. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience teaching relevant lecture and/or lab courses Graduate-level and/or postgraduate-level preparation in anatomy, physiology, or related Cadaver dissection and teaching experience Experience supervising students or teaching assistants Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the Faculty Academic/Administrative Information form. Attach the following documents: A cover letter highlighting the candidate’s interests and qualifications Curriculum Vitae A three-page teaching statement (Uploaded as “Other Document” The names and contact information for three references The teaching statement should summarize instructional experiences related to the position, teaching philosophy, and instructional methods as well as strategies for supporting students of all backgrounds. Although this is a teaching focused position, the successful candidate is expected to maintain research and/or scholarly activity. The teaching statement should therefore include a paragraph about how your research interests, background, and plans complement your teaching interests. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Brooke Crawley, badam2@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Non-Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
