    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102817": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - School of Computing",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant/Associate Professor - School of Computing Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor - School of Computing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Rolling reviews will continue until the position has been filled. Interested applicants are encouraged to continue to apply after the review of applications date. Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty information form, and attach the following documents: Cover letter explaining your interest in the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Curriculum vitae. A statement describing your research and scholarly activities, future directions, and broader impacts. A statement describing your teaching and mentoring practices. A statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the COE Complete Engineer ® Program ( engineering.unl.edu/complete-engineer ). A list of at least three (3) professional references including contact information. The statements for items 3, 4, and 5 together should total no more than six (6) pages. Please combine them into a single document and attach as \"Other Document.\" For more information about the position, please contact Dr. Brittany Duncan, bduncan@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor - School of Computing Department School of Computing-9301 Requisition Number F_260121 Posting Open Date 10/13/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 01/15/2027 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The School of Computing (SoC) at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln ( UNL ) is undergoing strategic expansion and invites applications for a tenured/tenure-track faculty position at the assistant or associate professor rank to begin in Fall 2027. SoC offers a collegial, collaborative culture and broad opportunities for interdisciplinary research across campus. We seek exceptional candidates who can establish a substantial scholarly research and teaching program in Robotics, with particular emphasis on the validation and verification of software systems that control safety-critical and mission-critical functionalities in autonomous aerial and ground vehicles. Areas of interest include formal methods, model-based design, software assurance, testing, verification, validation, runtime monitoring, digital twins, simulation-based evaluation, and certification of autonomous and robotic systems. The successful candidate will advance the dependability, safety, security, and resilience of software that enables perception, planning, decision-making, navigation, and control in next-generation autonomous vehicles and robotic platforms operating in complex and dynamic environments. Position Description The successful applicant will work in a team environment whose mission is to develop robotic systems to interact closely with the natural and built environment while working with end users of these systems. The successful candidate will be expected to develop a high-impact, nationally recognized research program in a self-identified area of applied robotics research or another closely related area. They will be expected to effectively obtain and leverage external and internal support for research; work with interdisciplinary teams; mentor students; publish in high-quality, high-impact peer-reviewed conferences and journals; and participate in scientific meetings and other appropriate professional activities. The successful candidate will have strong electrical, computing, and/or mechanical engineering skills and be interested in developing a collaborative program of applied research in robotics. For example, this may include sensor development, applied robotic perception, algorithm development, or other areas of interest. To support early-career success, the position includes a competitive startup package designed to establish a strong research program. This package provides funding for equipment, graduate student support, and research expenses, along with a reduced teaching load during the initial years. The successful candidate will also have access to modern laboratory space in our state-of-the-art facilities and shared resources, including advanced computational infrastructure provided through Holland Computing Center (hcc.unl.edu). School of Computing Overview The SoC is undergoing an exciting period of significant growth and has hired 14 tenured/tenure-track faculty members since 2019. We are committed to promoting inclusive excellence of our faculty and seek to attract and retain a high-performing and diverse workforce in which employees’ differences are respected and valued to meet the varying needs of the diverse populations we serve. The NIMBUS lab in SoC excels at developing Uncrewed Aircraft Systems for agricultural and scientific applications and also contributes to the $25 million Heartland Robotics Cluster. SoC is enhancing research in Data Science, AI, and Machine Learning, launching a new Data Science undergraduate major, and aiming to develop leading programs in health, agriculture, biocomputing, and robotics. The school also leads a Cybersecurity Initiative to tackle security challenges with AI and ML techniques. Additionally, SoC is a leader in IoT and Agricultural IoT, spearheading the Nebraska IoT Initiative through a public-private partnership. This includes collaborations on major infrastructure projects and the formation of the interlocal agency iLNK. Furthermore, SoC is also recognized for its work in Empirical Software Engineering, Testing, and Formal Methods, and is expanding into areas like Mining Software Repositories, Software Security, and Human-centered Software Engineering. College Growth The College of Engineering has hired more than 70 new faculty members over the past five years and continues to grow its faculty base to support future expansion. The School of Computing is central to advancing the College’s ambitious research goals, supported by state-of-the-art facilities, including a new $75 million research building and a $115 million engineering education building that opened in 2024. The College is committed to providing a world-class engineering education through initiatives such as the nationally recognized Complete Engineer® Program. Notably, UNL’s College of Engineering was among the first three institutions in the country to earn the ASEE Diversity Recognition Program Silver Award. We are seeking an innovative leader with a clear vision for growth and a strong commitment to excellence in research, education, and engagement within the School of Computing. About UNL , Lincoln, and Omaha The University of Nebraska-Lincoln is Nebraska’s land-grant research university, is a member of the Big Ten, and ranks among Doctoral Universities with the Highest Research Activity [Carnegie CIHE ]. As the state’s flagship institution, UNL plays a key role in the region’s research and innovation landscape and leverages CoE presence in Lincoln and Omaha. The city of Omaha, the largest metropolitan area in Nebraska, is a rising tech hub in the Midwest. Lincoln, the state capital, is also part of a growing high-tech region known as the ‘Midwest Silicon Prairie’. Taking advantage of both communities, UNL offers a vibrant, welcoming, family-friendly community with a strong economy, excellent public school systems, a modest cost of living, and a high quality of life. Learn more about life in Lincoln and Omaha at placetobelnk.com , aboutlincoln.unl.edu , and visitomaha.com . Minimum Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a related field by the start date of the appointment. Demonstrated research expertise in robotics, autonomous systems, perception, human-robot interactions, software engineering, or closely related areas. Evidence of high scholarly productivity (e.g., peer-reviewed publications). Evidence of or potential to establish and sustain an externally funded research program. A demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education. Preferred Qualifications Experience in the development and offering of innovative undergraduate and graduate courses. Potential to contribute to curriculum innovation and program development in robotics, computer science, or computer engineering. Experience collaborating on interdisciplinary research teams or with industry, federal agencies, or national laboratories. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Rolling reviews will continue until the position has been filled. Interested applicants are encouraged to continue to apply after the review of applications date. Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty information form, and attach the following documents: Cover letter explaining your interest in the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Curriculum vitae. A statement describing your research and scholarly activities, future directions, and broader impacts. A statement describing your teaching and mentoring practices. A statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the COE Complete Engineer ® Program ( engineering.unl.edu/complete-engineer ). A list of at least three (3) professional references including contact information. The statements for items 3, 4, and 5 together should total no more than six (6) pages. Please combine them into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” For more information about the position, please contact Dr. Brittany Duncan, bduncan@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Dr. Brittany Duncan bduncan@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/16/2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102806": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Postdoctoral Associate Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Postdoctoral Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty/administrative information form. Submit the following materials via www.mathjobs.org : A letter of application. Curriculum vitae. Statements addressing research and teaching. At least three letters of reference, at least one of which should address the applicant’s teachings. Please arrange for your references to submit their letters using www.mathjobs.org . Failure to submit applications to both www.mathjobs.org and https://employment.unl.edu will result in an incomplete application. Questions should be directed to the Chair of the RTG Postdoctoral Search Committee, Mark Walker, at mark.walker@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Postdoctoral Associate Department Mathematics-1088 Requisition Number F_260116 Posting Open Date 10/08/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Mathematics at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln invites applications for a three-year non-tenure track NSF -funded RTG postdoctoral faculty position, starting in August 2027. The NSF requires RTG postdocs to be US citizens or permanent residents. Responsibilities include research, teaching two courses per academic year, and running a year-long research seminar, with the help of a research mentor, during the second year in the position. UNL makes available reasonably priced life, health, and long-term disability insurance programs. To learn more about the department please visit https://math.unl.edu/ . Minimum Required Qualifications US citizen or permanent resident ( NSF requirement). Ph.D. or equivalent in mathematics or a closely related field or anticipated degree by August 2027. Preferred Qualifications Documented research activity and interests in commutative algebra, algebraic geometry, or related fields. Documented record of success in classroom instruction at the college level. Commitment to an inclusive environment and working with diverse communities. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty/administrative information form. Submit the following materials via www.mathjobs.org : A letter of application. Curriculum vitae. Statements addressing research and teaching. At least three letters of reference, at least one of which should address the applicant’s teachings. Please arrange for your references to submit their letters using www.mathjobs.org . Failure to submit applications to both www.mathjobs.org and https://employment.unl.edu will result in an incomplete application. Questions should be directed to the Chair of the RTG Postdoctoral Search Committee, Mark Walker, at mark.walker@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Mark Walker mark.walker@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Post Docs & Other Academic Job Type Full-Time Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/16/2027 Appointment End Date 05/10/2030 Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Due to NSF requirements, you must be a US Citizen or have permanent residency. Can you meet this requirement? Yes No Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102801": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Software Engineering",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant or Associate Professor - Software Engineering Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant or Associate Professor - Software Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Rolling reviews will continue until the position has been filled. Interested applicants are encouraged to continue to apply after the review of applications date. Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty information form, and attach the following documents: Cover letter explaining your interest in the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Curriculum vitae. A statement describing your research and scholarly activities, future directions, and broader impacts. A statement describing your teaching and mentoring practices. A statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the COE Complete Engineer ® Program ( engineering.unl.edu/complete-engineer ). A list of at least three (3) professional references including contact information. The statements for items 3, 4, and 5 together should total no more than six (6) pages. Please combine them into a single document and attach as \"Other Document.\" For questions or more information about the position, please contact the Chair of the Faculty Search Committee, Dr. Hamid Bagheri, bagheri@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor - Software Engineering Department School of Computing-9301 Requisition Number F_260120 Posting Open Date 10/12/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 01/15/2027 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The School of Computing (SoC) at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln ( UNL ) is undergoing strategic expansion and invites applications for a tenured/tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank to begin in Fall 2027. SoC offers a collegial, collaborative culture and broad opportunities for interdisciplinary research across campus. We seek exceptional candidates who can establish a substantial scholarly research and teaching program in Software Engineering focused on improving the dependability, safety, and/or security of AI-based software systems. The successful candidate will join a rapidly growing Software Engineering community with opportunities to collaborate across AI, cybersecurity, robotics, agriculture, health, and data science initiatives at UNL . Position Description The successful candidate will pursue a strong research program in Software Engineering, with particular emphasis on methods, tools, and foundations for improving the dependability, safety, and security of AI-based software systems. We are especially interested in research addressing the design, development, testing, verification, validation, deployment, and evolution of software incorporating machine learning and deep learning models, generative AI and large language models, AI agents and agentic systems, autonomous systems, and cyber-physical systems. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, testing and debugging of AI-enabled software; verification and validation of learning-enabled and agentic systems; formal methods and software assurance for trustworthy AI; safety, security, and reliability of autonomous and cyber-physical systems; explainability and interpretability as they relate to software assurance; integration of assurance techniques into modern software engineering workflows; and program analysis and other software engineering techniques for improving system dependability. While these areas are of particular interest, we welcome applicants whose research spans the broader field of Software Engineering. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain a vigorous, externally funded research program in Software Engineering or a closely related area. They will contribute to both undergraduate and graduate education through teaching of core courses in our Software Engineering program, mentoring graduate and undergraduate researchers, and offering courses aligned with their area of expertise. Additional responsibilities include active participation in school, college, and university governance, contributions to curriculum development, and engagement in interdisciplinary collaborations with partners across campus as well as in industry, government, and national laboratories. Candidates at the Associate Professor rank should demonstrate a sustained record of scholarly achievement, research leadership, external funding, graduate student mentoring, and national or international visibility in their field. To support research success, the position includes a competitive startup package designed to establish a strong research program. This package provides funding for equipment, graduate student support, and research expenses, along with a reduced teaching load during the initial years. The successful candidate will also have access to modern laboratory space in our state-of-the-art facilities and shared departmental resources, including advanced computational infrastructure provided through Holland Computing Center ( hcc.unl.edu ). School of Computing Overview The SoC is undergoing an exciting period of significant growth and has hired 14 tenured/tenure-track faculty members since 2019. We are committed to promoting excellence among our faculty and seek to attract and retain a high-performing workforce in which employees’ differences are respected and valued to meet the varying needs of the populations we serve. SoC is recognized for its work in Empirical Software Engineering, Testing, Formal Methods, and Mining Software Repositories, and is expanding into areas such as Software Security, Software Engineering in Robotics, and Human-centered Software Engineering. SoC is enhancing research in Data Science, AI, and Machine Learning, recently introducing a new Data Science undergraduate major, Artificial Intelligence (AI) Master’s degree and Graduate Certificate program, and undergraduate AI minor, aiming to develop impactful programs in health, agriculture, biocomputing, and robotics. The school also leads a Cybersecurity Initiative to tackle security challenges with AI and ML techniques. Additionally, SoC is a leader in IoT and Agricultural IoT, spearheading the Nebraska IoT Initiative through a public-private partnership. This includes collaborations on significant infrastructure projects and the formation of the interlocal agency iLNK. Furthermore, the NIMBUS lab excels at developing Uncrewed Aircraft Systems for agricultural and scientific applications and contributes to the $25 million Heartland Robotics Cluster. College Growth The College of Engineering has hired more than 70 new faculty members over the past five years and continues to grow its faculty base to support future expansion. The School of Computing is central to advancing the College’s ambitious research goals, supported by state-of-the-art facilities, including newly renovated research facilities for robotics, virtual/augmented reality, wireless communications, and IoT devices. The college recently unveiled a new $75 million research building and a $115 million engineering education building. The College is committed to providing a world-class engineering education through initiatives such as the nationally recognized Complete Engineer® Program. We are seeking an innovative leader with a clear vision for growth and a strong commitment to excellence in research, education, and engagement within the School of Computing. About UNL , Lincoln, and Omaha The University of Nebraska-Lincoln is Nebraska’s land-grant research university, a member of the Big Ten, and ranks among Doctoral Universities with the Highest Research Activity [Carnegie CIHE ]. As the state’s flagship institution, UNL plays a key role in the region’s research and innovation landscape and leverages the College of Engineering’s presence in Lincoln and Omaha. The city of Omaha, the largest metropolitan area in Nebraska, is a rising tech hub in the Midwest. Lincoln, the state capital, is also part of a growing high-tech region known as the ‘Midwest Silicon Prairie’. Taking advantage of both communities, UNL offers a vibrant, welcoming, family-friendly community with a strong economy, excellent public school systems, a modest cost of living, and a high quality of life. Learn more about life in Lincoln and Omaha at visitomaha.com , placetobelnk.com , and aboutlincoln.unl.edu . The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination . Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a related field by the start date of the appointment. Demonstrated research expertise in software engineering or a closely related area, including software security, programming languages, artificial intelligence, or other areas relevant to the development of dependable, safe, and secure software systems. Evidence of high scholarly productivity (e.g., peer-reviewed publications). Evidence of or potential to establish and sustain an externally funded research program. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education. Preferred Qualifications Research expertise aligned with Software Engineering for dependable, safe, and secure AI-enabled, autonomous, or software-intensive systems. Experience in the development and offering of innovative undergraduate and graduate courses. Potential to contribute to curriculum innovation and program development in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or Data Science. Experience collaborating on interdisciplinary research teams or with industry, federal agencies, or national laboratories. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Rolling reviews will continue until the position has been filled. Interested applicants are encouraged to continue to apply after the review of applications date. Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty information form, and attach the following documents: Cover letter explaining your interest in the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Curriculum vitae. A statement describing your research and scholarly activities, future directions, and broader impacts. A statement describing your teaching and mentoring practices. A statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the COE Complete Engineer ® Program ( engineering.unl.edu/complete-engineer ). A list of at least three (3) professional references including contact information. The statements for items 3, 4, and 5 together should total no more than six (6) pages. Please combine them into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” For questions or more information about the position, please contact the Chair of the Faculty Search Committee, Dr. Hamid Bagheri, bagheri@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Dr. Hamid Bagheri bagheri@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/16/2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102794": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Human Dimensions",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Postdoctoral Research Associate - Human Dimensions Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Postdoctoral Research Associate - Human Dimensions Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A letter of interest that describes your qualifications for the position and career aspirations, as well as your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments where every person and every interaction matters. See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three (3) professional references. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Postdoctoral Research Associate - Human Dimensions Department School of Natural Resources-0844 Requisition Number F_260088 Posting Open Date 09/10/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/19/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The School of Natural Resources at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources ( IANR ) is seeking applications for two highly motivated and enthusiastic postdoctoral research associates. These are 12-month (calendar year), 100% research special appointments located in Lincoln, Nebraska, with remote work negotiable. One postdoc will be working within an interdisciplinary team to develop and implement social science indicators focused on stakeholder and community well-being within the Central Plains. The other postdoc will be working within an interdisciplinary team to develop and implement social science related to amplification/diffusion of collaborative adaptive rangeland management. Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources ( IANR ) and the School of Natural Resources are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR , we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission. In addition to the above-described duties, the individuals will be expected to accept committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in human dimensions of natural resources/agriculture, sociology, or a closely related field. Experience in interview, focus group, and/or survey design, implementation, and analysis. Strong writing skills with demonstrated ability to publish manuscripts in peer reviewed journals. Preferred Qualifications Expertise in U.S. ranching social-ecological systems. Expertise in social network analysis. Strong verbal communication skills. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A letter of interest that describes your qualifications for the position and career aspirations, as well as your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments where every person and every interaction matters. See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three (3) professional references. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Marci Sturek msturek2@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Post Docs & Other Academic Job Type 12 Month (Faculty Only) Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102773": {
      "title": "Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - HLES Urban Entomology (Lancaster County)",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - HLES Urban Entomology (Lancaster County) Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - HLES Urban Entomology (Lancaster County) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty information form, and attach: A letter of interest that describes your qualifications for the job and anticipated contributions. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references. In addition, please complete the required supplemental question(s) within the application, one specifically describing your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments where every person and every interaction matters. See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Extension Instructor or Open Rank Extension Educator - HLES Urban Entomology (Lancaster County) Department NE Ext Engagement Zone 9-12358 Requisition Number F_260119 Posting Open Date 10/08/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work This is a full-time, 12-month non-tenured position based in Lincoln, NE with a geographic accountability region including Lancaster, Cass, Otoe, Seward and York Counties . The subject matter focus for this Extension professional is horticulture, landscapes and environmental systems ( HLES ) with a primary focus on Urban Entomology with an emphasis on plant and food insect issues as well as those insects that affect humans like head lice and bed bugs. This education professional’s primary responsibility is to develop and deliver educational programs and resources as an active participant in Nebraska Extension’s statewide mission. They will work closely with individuals, homeowners, producers, institutions, and organizations in communities to deliver programs in their geographic area and statewide, based on the statewide program area team’s priorities. The HLES Extension professional will contribute to the integrated extension land-grant mission of the home unit and the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources ( IANR ) as an effective scholar and citizen, including support for student recruitment and IANR science literacy efforts in entomology-related initiatives. In HLES we educate and engage Nebraskans, including pest control companies, and property managers, to protect natural resources and habitats, sustainably manage community spaces, be better consumers, and make wise business decisions. Nebraska Extension is an organization that values excellence; as a member of the Nebraska Extension team, you are expected to create and deliver world-class learning experiences focused on critical issues that empower Nebraskans to improve their lives. Expected impacts from this position: Nebraskans will adopt environmentally and economically sustainable integrated best pest management practices to address and reduce pests in urban areas. Nebraskans will increase awareness and adoption of best pest management practices for high-priority invasive and emerging insect pests such as, but not limited to, emerald ash borer, Japanese beetles, bed bugs, ticks and head lice. Nebraskans will adopt practices that enhance beneficial insect ecosystems. Programmatic Responsibilities (approximately 80%): Exemplifies positive and professional behavior and attitude towards colleagues, clients, and partner organizations. Develops and delivers proactive, innovative, and engaging educational programs and products, using teaching methods and strategies that have significant reach, engagement, and impact in your county, accountability region, and, as appropriate, statewide and nationally. Establishes and sustains a strong local and regional clientele base and programming portfolio that is documented and shared with colleagues. Employs innovative strategies and technologies to design, develop, implement, and assess programs for a strong Extension education program/engagement at the county, accountability region, and statewide levels. Engages and teaches in a collaborative learning and problem-solving environment, working with assistants, educators, and specialists to encourage learners to adopt research-based decision-making information. Deliberately engages and works closely with one or more Extension specialists to fulfill your Extension responsibilities. Collaborates with specialists and research faculty to conduct applied and validation research (e.g., landscape or community) that can be amplified via multiple engagement platforms. Shows robust contributions to multidisciplinary team settings with Extension professionals and other internal and external partners to translate and convey the latest research-based information. Engages local, regional, and statewide partners to identify and address high-priority issues where Extension is particularly well positioned to contribute. Fosters a culture of collaboration with local, regional and statewide leaders that nurtures and strengthens positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the people we serve. Employs innovative, revenue-generating practices to secure funding and develop partnerships that expand Extension program’s reach and impact. Creates ongoing programming revenue that supports the viability of individuals, teams, units, and the System. Leads and contributes value to high-performing Extension programming teams. Engages in personal and professional development opportunities that enhance knowledge, skills, and competencies relevant to your role. Supports youth development programs by contributing to areas related to your specific assignment. Conducts need assessments, identifies priorities, develops various program and engagement platforms to connect with a variety of audiences, measure program impact, and report the results in your annual report as well as to Extension boards, County Commissioners and Supervisors, State Senators, key stakeholders, at professional meetings, and in professional and Extension publications when appropriate. Educators will collaborate with lead educators, Extension specialists, Extension advisory committees, and local stakeholders within their accountability region to assess needs and offer access to engagement opportunities through various platforms (e.g., focus groups, surveys, stakeholder meetings, etc.). Participates in teams comprised of assistants, educators, specialists, other staff or faculty, industry, and community leaders. These teams focus on current or future needs or strengths and strategize in program areas where you contribute. Fosters a culture of collaboration with local leaders and accountability in the region that nurtures and builds positive relationships among the University, its partners, and the communities we serve. Cultivates open and welcoming learning environments. Completes PEARS data entry and reporting requirements. Fulfills annual IANR reporting requirements, including an individual impact report. Organizational Citizenship (approximately 20%): Contributes to and supports the Lead Educator as described in the Roles and Responsibilities of the Lead Educator document as determined in partnership with the supervisor(s). Coordinates with engagement zone coordinator(s) and other Extension professionals locally and in accountability region to develop a robust Nebraska Extension presence by Cooperating with local faculty and staff in a team environment to promote Extension’s educational opportunities and impact in the host county. Cultivating a culture of collaboration with local leaders and community members that builds positive relationships between the University and the community. Supporting the engagement of advisory or policy groups such as the Extension Board, Ag Society, or County Commissioners/Board of Supervisors. Understands and adheres to Equal Employment Opportunity compliance efforts. Accepts committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college, division, institute, and/or university level. This twelve-month, non-tenure position carries the title of open rank extension educator or extension instructor, depending on the candidate’s level of education. Those possessing a graduate level degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an open rank educator position, a full-time, promotable, non-tenure track appointment. Those in possession of an undergraduate degree in the requested area of instruction will be considered for an instructor position, a full-time, non-promotable, non-tenure track appointment that will be renewed annually for a maximum of five years in the appointment. If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress towards and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. As part of the Nebraska benefits package, UNL offers tuition remission for full-time employees, up to 15 credit hours per year. Once the master’s degree is earned within that period, the position will advance to an assistant extension educator appointment. Some travel is required. Must meet driver standards according to UNL policy and have a valid driver’s license. Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact and a sense of belonging, the IANR and Nebraska Extension are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR , we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission. This position is not eligible for employment-based permanent residency sponsorship. UNL may be able to sponsor a temporary work authorization (e.g., H-1B) for the successful candidate. Minimum Required Qualifications Master’s degree in entomology or closely related field (extension educator) OR bachelor’s degree in entomology or closely related field (extension instructor). If hired as an instructor, the incumbent will be expected to make satisfactory progress towards and complete a master’s degree within the initial five-year appointment period. Successful experience teaching in a formal or non-formal setting. Demonstrated ability to communicate (i.e., publications, presentations, web, and social media). Experience with and/or teaching urban pest management. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with individuals, coworkers, and teams to accomplish individual and/or group goals, as evidenced by college, career, and/or community activities. Outstanding leadership skills as demonstrated by roles in college, career, and/or community activities. Ability to utilize electronic and online technologies for educational program delivery. Successful experience in developing financial support for educational programs including grant writing, fund generation, contracting and/or cost recovery efforts. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty information form, and attach: A letter of interest that describes your qualifications for the job and anticipated contributions. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references. In addition, please complete the required supplemental question(s) within the application, one specifically describing your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments where every person and every interaction matters. See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Marci Sturek msturek2@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Non-Tenure Leading Job Type 12 Month (Faculty Only) Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Provide a statement describing your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments in which every person and every interaction matters. (Open Ended Question) * What qualities do you have that make you an effective team player? (Open Ended Question) * Identify formal classwork, professional development, or continuing education in the past 5 years relevant to this position. (Open Ended Question) * Describe your experiences working with organizations, businesses, agencies, or individuals in horticulture-related activities within the past five years. (Open Ended Question) Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102766": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A cover letter. Current CV. A statement of research interests. Samples of recent work. A teaching statement in which applicants may include evidence of teaching and teaching effectiveness. Combine items 3, 4, and 5 into a single document and upload as “Other Document.” The combined document must not exceed 9 MB. Additionally, three (3) letters of reference should be submitted through the JOE system ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/reference-letter-writers/ ). Completed applications must be received by the application review date to be guaranteed full consideration, but will be accepted until the position is filled or the search closed. The Department will be interviewing selected candidates via Zoom sessions beginning in December 2026. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant Professor Department Economics-1024 Requisition Number F_260117 Posting Open Date 10/09/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/11/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Economics Department is seeking a tenure-track Assistant Professor in applied microeconomics beginning August 2027. The successful candidate is expected to develop an outstanding research program in applied microeconomics, provide excellent teaching, and supervise undergraduate and graduate student research. The University of Nebraska-Lincoln is home to a Federal Statistical Research Data Center ( RDC – https://www.census.gov/fsrdc ) which provides researchers with access to restricted federal micro-level data from the Census and other federal agencies. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to develop research projects using RDC data. About the College of Business The College of Business drives discovery, creates opportunity, and empowers its record-breaking 4,534 students to lead the future of business. Programs include 12 undergraduate majors and numerous graduate programs, including our highly-ranked online MBA , three online master of science degrees, and two Ph.D. programs. Established in 1913, it is the only doctorate granting business college in Nebraska. Howard L. Hawks Hall, located at 14th and Vine Streets, has been home to the college since 2017. Hawks Hall features interactive learning in state-of-the-art classrooms, cutting-edge technology and one-stop student support services, including free one-on-one tutoring and coaching. For more information, visit https://business.unl.edu/ . About the University of Nebraska–Lincoln We are proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and certified as a Family Friendly Workplace. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. About Lincoln, Nebraska Home to the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, the city of Lincoln consistently ranks one of the happiest cities in America and highest for livability thanks to a low cost of living, great schools and friendly, community-minded residents. Set amidst a big sky and open landscape, the state’s capital city is simple to navigate with a nationally noted low crime rate, a wide range of housing choices and a reliable public transit system. As one of the fastest growing metro areas in the Midwest, Lincoln boasts a growing technology sector, more parkland per capita than all but a few U.S. cities, an extensive bike trail network, and numerous options for recreational and personal interest activities. It’s easy to feel at home here. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Economics at the beginning of the appointment. Strong background in applied microeconomics, with research interests that include an emphasis on empirical analysis. Ability to contribute to the department’s delivery of courses in public economics broadly defined. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of research excellence in public economics or related fields complementary to the department’s other focus areas, including labor and international. Interest in working with the RDC . Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A cover letter. Current CV. A statement of research interests. Samples of recent work. A teaching statement in which applicants may include evidence of teaching and teaching effectiveness. Combine items 3, 4, and 5 into a single document and upload as “Other Document.” The combined document must not exceed 9 MB. Additionally, three (3) letters of reference should be submitted through the JOE system ( https://www.aeaweb.org/joe/reference-letter-writers/ ). Completed applications must be received by the application review date to be guaranteed full consideration, but will be accepted until the position is filled or the search closed. The Department will be interviewing selected candidates via Zoom sessions beginning in December 2026. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Direct questions about the position to search chair Sam Allgood ( allgood@unl.edu ). Direct questions about the application process to Phyllis Schwab ( phyllis.schwab@unl.edu ). Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102755": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Engineering Education",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant or Associate Professor - Engineering Education Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant or Associate Professor - Engineering Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the information form. Attach the following documents: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae . Research statement (2 pages max) Teaching statement (2 pages max) A statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the COE Complete Engineer® program ( https://engineering.unl.edu/complete-engineer/) (2 pages max). A list of three references. References will not be contacted until the final interview round. Please combine the research, teaching, and COE Complete Engineer® statements into a single pdf document and attach as “Other Document.” Review of application materials will begin November 9, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For more information, please contact Dr. Grace Panther, Associate Professor and Search Chair, at grace.panther@unl.edu. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor - Engineering Education Department College of Engineering-0907 Requisition Number F_260104 Posting Open Date 10/08/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The College of Engineering (CoE) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln (https://engineering.unl.edu) is seeking applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of assistant or associate professor in the area of engineering education. The primary faculty appointment will be in one of the following academic units in the College of Engineering: Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Electrical & Computer Engineering, Durham School of Architectural Engineering and Construction (specifically Construction Management or Construction Engineering), depending on an applicant’s qualifications. Candidates selected will be expected to contribute to the academic programs in their CoE unit through teaching undergraduate courses as well as teaching graduate-level engineering education courses and supervising graduate research within the PhD in Engineering – Specialization in Engineering Education Research program. Candidates will be expected to establish externally funded discipline-based education research ( DBER ) programs and collaborate with researchers within CoE to study and transform engineering education through fundamental and applied research. The DBER initiative at UNL’s College of Engineering (https://dber-engr.unl.edu/) boasts four tenured or tenure-track faculty members and 6 PhD alumni since our program’s launch in 2020. DBER faculty reside in their respective disciplines where, through their presence and participation on their faculties, they build relationships and collaborations with their disciplinary colleagues to conduct engineering discipline-specific education research that focuses on aspects unique to the education and preparation of professionals in their discipline. DBER faculty also operate as a community to conduct cross-disciplinary engineering education research focused on aspects common to the education and preparation of all engineering professionals. Minimum Required Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent in an engineering discipline (including engineering education) or a closely related field, with a bachelor’s and/or master’s degree in an engineering discipline. Applicants must have doctoral training that emphasized rigorous engineering education research practices and/or have an established track record in engineering education research. Applicants must have a record of strong scholarly achievement. Applicants must have a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education commensurate to the position level they are applying for. Applicants must have the potential to establish a strong externally funded research program. Individuals under consideration for appointment at the Associate Professor level are expected to satisfy the University’s requirements, as well as the applicable unit-level standards, for tenure and promotion at that rank. In general, candidates should demonstrate a sustained research program, a strong body of peer-reviewed publications, success in securing external research support, and a consistent record of effective teaching and mentorship. Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience at the undergraduate and/or graduate level Experience conducting discipline-based education research Experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students This position is open to all research areas within engineering education; we are particularly interested in those whose research uses machine learning, deep learning, large language models, generative AI, or advanced quantitative methods to answer critical research questions. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the information form. Attach the following documents: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae . Research statement (2 pages max) Teaching statement (2 pages max) A statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the COE Complete Engineer® program ( https://engineering.unl.edu/complete-engineer/) (2 pages max). A list of three references. References will not be contacted until the final interview round. Please combine the research, teaching, and COE Complete Engineer® statements into a single pdf document and attach as “Other Document.” Review of application materials will begin November 9, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For more information, please contact Dr. Grace Panther, Associate Professor and Search Chair, at grace.panther@unl.edu. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact For more information, please contact Dr. Grace Panther, Associate Professor and Search Chair at grace.panther@unl.edu. Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/16/2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102751": {
      "title": "Asst/Assoc Professor - Secondary Mathematics Education",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Asst/Assoc Professor - Secondary Mathematics Education Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Asst/Assoc Professor - Secondary Mathematics Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty application, and attach the following: Letter of application outlining your qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae. Teaching statement. Research statement. Two examples of scholarly work. Transcripts or unofficial copies of transcripts from the doctoral program (official copies of transcripts will be required at time of offer). Contact information for three professional references who will be contacted and/or asked to provide letters of recommendation. Combine documents 3, 4, 5, and 6 into a single document and attach as \"Other Document.\" Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Asst/Assoc Professor - Secondary Mathematics Education Department Teaching, Learning & Teacher Ed-1045 Requisition Number F_260102 Posting Open Date 10/05/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Teaching, Learning and Teacher Education ( https://cehs.unl.edu/tlte ) seeks a tenure-line Assistant or Associate Professor of Secondary Mathematics Education who can help prepare effective educators; collaborate with department colleagues, mathematics and STEM content specialists, and classroom teachers, and attract increased national interest and funding to nationally visible programs in mathematics education at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Our new colleague will be joining a dynamic and committed community of scholars in the department and a collaborative faculty group in secondary education. The program graduates 10-12 teacher candidates yearly and graduate math education courses that enroll 10-27 in-service teachers each during academic year semesters and during summer terms. Our programs benefit from long-standing and unique partnerships with the Department of Mathematics in the College of Arts and Sciences and the Center for Science, Mathematics, and Computer Education. We anticipate expanding our faculty in elementary, secondary, and mathematics education not only to prepare students for initial teacher certification, but also to provide professional learning in graduate education and expand opportunities for funded research and scholarship. UNL is the University of Nebraska system’s flagship university and a member of the Big 10 Academic Alliance. TLTE is recognized across UNL for distinguished teaching, strong collaborations with exceptional partner schools and has a reputation for scholarship that embraces diverse research methodologies. The candidate who fills this position will teach and advise undergraduate and graduate students in mathematics education. TLTE seeks a colleague who possess the understanding, commitment, and ability to contribute collaboratively to robust elementary and secondary education programs and mathematics education in the context of continuing demographic change in the state and nation. The College of Education and Human Sciences strives to be a vibrant, welcoming, and caring community driven by our mission to enhance the lives of individuals, families, schools, and communities, and strengthening the relationships among them. At the University of Nebraska, we strive for excellence in all that we do. True excellence requires that every individual is able to work and learn in an atmosphere of respect, dignity, and acceptance. Our commitment requires each of us to continuously ensure our interactions be respectful, protect free speech, and inspire academic freedom. Position Responsibilities Teach undergraduate coursework in Secondary Mathematics Education, including mathematics methods courses. Work with and supervise professional practicum students and student teachers. Teach graduate courses in K-12 Mathematics Education and related areas of expertise. Advise and mentor master’s and doctoral students. Conduct a scholarly program of research appropriate to rank. Engage actively in collaboration and program development within and across content areas, programs, departments and colleges. Provide outreach to schools, other educational institutions, and communities. For additional questions, please contact Dr. Amanda Henson, Search Committee Chair, at amanda.thomas@unl.edu . Minimum Required Qualifications Assistant Professor Level Doctorate in mathematics education, curriculum & instruction, teacher education, or a related field. Demonstrated expertise in the teaching of mathematics education in higher education and supervising teacher candidates in practicum and student teaching settings. A minimum of two (2) years of teaching experience in secondary mathematics education. A research agenda anchored in secondary mathematics education and/or mathematics teacher education that is commensurate with expectations of a research-intensive institution. Evidence of professional and institutional service. Demonstrated commitment to access and equity in teaching and scholarship. Associate Professor Level Doctorate in mathematics education, curriculum & instruction, teacher education, or a related field. Demonstrated excellence in the teaching of mathematics education in higher education. A minimum of two (2) years of teaching experience in secondary mathematics education. An established research agenda anchored in secondary mathematics education and/or mathematics teacher education, with a sustained record of scholarly productivity commensurate with expectations of a research-intensive institution. Evidence of an emerging or established national reputation in secondary mathematics education and/or mathematics teacher education. Demonstrated experience mentoring and advising undergraduate and/or graduate students. A sustained record of professional and institutional service in higher education. Academic credentials and accomplishments commensurate with appointment at the rank of Associate Professor at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Preferred Qualifications Assistant Professor Level Demonstrated mentoring and advising abilities. Experience teaching at the college level. Experience teaching courses in a variety of formats (e.g., in person, online, hybrid, site-based). Participation in funded projects (particularly in seeking and/or securing external funding). Demonstrated success working with students from diverse cultures and backgrounds. Experience in secondary mathematics program/course development. Associate Professor Level Demonstrated success mentoring and advising master’s and doctoral students. A record of securing or contributing substantially to externally funded projects. Experience leading collaborative research, program development, or professional learning initiatives. Experience teaching courses in a variety of formats (e.g., in person, online, hybrid, site-based). Demonstrated success working with students from diverse cultures and backgrounds. Experience developing or strengthening secondary mathematics education programs and courses. Evidence of successful collaboration with schools, school districts, professional organizations, and university-based colleagues. A record of leadership and service at the state, regional, and/or national level. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty application, and attach the following: Letter of application outlining your qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae. Teaching statement. Research statement. Two examples of scholarly work. Transcripts or unofficial copies of transcripts from the doctoral program (official copies of transcripts will be required at time of offer). Contact information for three professional references who will be contacted and/or asked to provide letters of recommendation. Combine documents 3, 4, 5, and 6 into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Dr. Amanda Henson Search Committee Chair amanda.thomas@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date August 16, 2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
