    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102731": {
      "title": "Reference Librarian - Open Rank Professor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Reference Librarian - Open Rank Professor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Reference Librarian - Open Rank Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following required documents. A letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. Names and contact information for three professional references. For questions about the application process, please contact Rich Leiter, Direcor of the Schmid Law Library, University of Nebraska College of Law, Lincoln, NE 68583-0902 at rich.leiter@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Reference Librarian - Open Rank Professor Department College of Law-0899 Requisition Number F_260110 Posting Open Date 10/07/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/23/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The University of Nebraska College of Law invites applications for the position of Reference Librarian (Open Rank Professor) at the Schmid Law Library. This 12-month, tenure-track law library faculty position offers an opportunity to support student learning and faculty scholarship while contributing to the mission and values of the College of Law. As a valued member of the law library faculty, the Reference Librarian/Law Library Professor will: Provide expert research assistance and reference services to a diverse community, including faculty, law students, graduate and undergraduate students, and the public. Teach in the first-year legal research program. Lead and participate in instructional and outreach initiatives. Demonstrate initiative in developing and implementing law library resources, such as creating Libguides and bibliographies that enhance research and learning. Take on evolving responsibilities within a modern law library, based on institutional priorities and an individual’s expertise and interests. Conduct or contribute to research, scholarship, and other significant creative activity. Promote a positive, collaborative, inclusive, and innovative work environment within the law library and the College of Law. This role offers an exciting opportunity to contribute meaningfully to legal education, research, and law library services in a dynamic academic setting. Members of the law library faculty participate in faculty governance at the College of Law and may apply for faculty development fellowships (sabbatical). Initial appointment and rank will be commensurate with experience. Law library faculty will participate in the University’s generous benefits package. Please find the full range of benefits at https://hr.unl.edu/health-benefits/ . General information about the Law College is available at https://law.unl.edu/ . Minimum Required Qualifications A Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an ABA -accredited law school and a Master’s Degree in Library and Information Science or equivalent degree from an ALA -accredited master’s program by the start of employment. OR A Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an ABA -accredited law school and current enrollment in a Master’s degree program in Library and Information Science from an ALA -accredited institution, or an equivalent graduate degree in library or information science, with completion required within 18 months of hire; or current enrollment in a joint degree program, with completion of both the J.D. and the Master’s degree within six months of hire. OR A Master’s Degree in Library and Information Science or equivalent degree from an ALA -accredited master’s program AND substantial professional experience as a law librarian demonstrating qualifications comparable to those described above. The title of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor will be based on the successful candidate’s qualifications. Preferred Qualifications Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following required documents. A letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. Names and contact information for three professional references. For questions about the application process, please contact Rich Leiter, Direcor of the Schmid Law Library, University of Nebraska College of Law, Lincoln, NE 68583-0902 at rich.leiter@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Rich Leiter rich.leiter@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type Full-Time Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102725": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor - Plant Metabolism",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Open Rank Professor - Plant Metabolism Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Open Rank Professor - Plant Metabolism Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and then “Faculty Application.” Complete the application and attach the following documents: A letter of interest that describes your qualifications for the job and anticipated contributions. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references. Statements that describe your philosophy and approach to teaching and research. A statement describing your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments in which every person and every interaction matters (2 page maximum). See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Please combine the statements (items 4 and 5) into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Open Rank Professor - Plant Metabolism Department Biochemistry-0831 Requisition Number F_260106 Posting Open Date 10/01/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 12/01/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Biochemistry and the Center for Plant Science Innovation at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) invite applications for a tenure-track nine-month (academic year) faculty position of open rank (assistant/associate/full professor). This appointment is apportioned as 80% research and 20% teaching. Applicants are sought who will develop a vigorous, internationally recognized research program that seeks to identify novel metabolic pathways, regulatory mechanisms and/or biological processes with the goal of translating findings into strategies for crop improvement and/or bio-based products that support sustainable agriculture and biotechnology to enhance human health. Researchers will be able to leverage UNL’s extensive research infrastructure that includes the Plant Transformation Core Research Facility ( PTCRF ), multi-location biotech fields, and advanced field and greenhouse phenotyping platforms, to validate and scale their discoveries. The Department of Biochemistry provides a robust environment for molecular research, offering access to state-of-the-art resources through shared equipment and the Nebraska Center for Biotechnology. Candidates will have the opportunity to utilize the UNL Cryo-EM facility for structural biology, mass spectrometry for metabolomics and proteomics, and bioinformatics and systems biology computational resources. The university offers a highly collaborative environment to develop plant-focused research programs with affiliated resources provided by the University Research Centers (Center for Plant Science Innovation, Center for Integrated Biomolecular Communication, Redox Biology Center, Center for Virology), Holland Computing Center, the Quantitative Life Sciences Initiative, Nebraska Innovation Campus and the Center for Biological Chemistry and Complex Biosystems graduate training programs. The University Research Centers and UNL provide cutting-edge research facilities that support multiple-omics, bioinformatics, supercomputing, flow cytometry, confocal microscopy, TEM , SEM , and metabolic engineering. A competitive start-up package and appropriate laboratory and office space will be offered. About Us To learn about UNL benefits and your total compensation, please see: https://go.unl.edu/aboutus . To learn more about Lincoln, NE at About Lincoln | Nebraska . Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent degree in biochemistry, plant science, or a related field. Two or more years of postdoctoral experience. Strong record of original research in plant biochemistry as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications. Preferred Qualifications Experience in grant writing. Experience teaching in biochemistry or related fields. Experience with mentoring students. Excellent communication skills. Expertise in integrated biochemical, structural, and molecular genetic approaches in plant metabolism. Demonstrated potential for collaborative research. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and then “Faculty Application.” Complete the application and attach the following documents: A letter of interest that describes your qualifications for the job and anticipated contributions. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references. Statements that describe your philosophy and approach to teaching and research. A statement describing your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments in which every person and every interaction matters (2 page maximum). See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Please combine the statements (items 4 and 5) into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Rachel Szelag, rszelag2@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102715": {
      "title": "Dean of the College of Journalism and Mass Communications",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Dean of the College of Journalism and Mass Communications Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Dean of the College of Journalism and Mass Communications Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We will begin reviewing candidates immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Priority consideration will be given to those materials received by November 9, 2026. Applications should consist of a letter summarizing motivation, relevant leadership experience, and qualifications and a detailed curriculum vitae. To apply, click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty application form, and upload the following materials: Letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. The names and contact information for at least three professional references will be requested from candidates who advance to the interview stages. Questions and nominations can be sent in confidence, to: Kathy Farrell, Search Chair James Jr. and Susan Stuart Endowed Dean, College of Business University of Nebraska-Lincoln kfarrell2@unl.edu and Allison Wortmann Academic Personnel and HR Specialist University of Nebraska-Lincoln allison.wortmann@unl.edu The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Dean of the College of Journalism and Mass Communications Department Journalism & Mass Comm-0908 Requisition Number F_260115 Posting Open Date 10/05/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The College of Journalism and Mass Communications The College of Journalism and Mass Communications is an inclusive community of faculty and staff committed to providing a top-quality, hands-on education to emerging professionals in advertising, broadcasting, journalism, public relations, and sports media and communication. The college is an important contributor to education, research, creative activity and outreach at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. The faculty upholds the core principles of journalism and mass communication education and seeks to be leaders in the evolving communications environment. Through excellence in teaching, research and creative activity, the college educates ethical, socially responsible, well-rounded, flexible, fair and quick-minded graduates who carry those traits into the world. The strength of the college is exemplified by the success of its students and graduates and its numerous professional partnerships. The college is one of 11 chosen to be part of the Carnegie-Knight Initiative on the Future of Journalism and the only collegiate recipient of the Robert F. Kennedy Journalism Grand Prize. Its students have consistently finished in the top 10 in the Hearst Journalism Awards annual competition; this year, students won 1st and 3rd place in the National Writing Championship. The college was also the 2022 national champion in the Public Relations Student Society of America Bateman Case Study Competition. The college programs have been nationally accredited by the Accrediting Council on Education in Journalism and Mass Communications since 1972 and are the only accredited journalism offerings in the state of Nebraska. It offers bachelor’s and master’s degree programs that prepare students for careers in a wide range of media positions. Enrollment in the college is approximately 1,100 undergraduate and 75 graduate students. Students experience a variety of special hands-on learning opportunities including: The Experience Lab where students gain hands-on experience working with faculty liaisons and professional mentors, building on their academic skill set while exploring their professional interests in one of the college’s media outlets; first-year learning communities; Jacht, a student-run advertising agency; 90.3 KRNU , a student-run FM radio station that just underwent an equipment upgrade; the Nebraska News Service, which provides state government coverage for smaller Nebraska newspapers and radio stations; an annual international photojournalism trip; investigative depth reporting such as a recent investigation into the Nebraska prison system; and an advertising and a public relations national competition team. The college has 35 full-time faculty members plus a large number of highly qualified part-time faculty from industry. The college faculty includes two Pulitzer Prize winners, recipients of Emmys in broadcasting and a National Gold ADDY award honoree. The journalism faculty includes veterans from Business Week, the Miami Herald, the Detroit News, ProPublica and the Tampa Bay Times. The broadcast faculty includes individuals who have held key positions with news stations in Omaha, Kansas City, and San Francisco. The advertising and public relations faculty includes former executives at Leo Burnett, J. Walter Thompson, IGN Entertainment, and the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers. The Opportunity The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks an innovative, inspiring and forward-looking academic leader to serve as the next Dean of the College of Journalism and Mass Communications. The incoming Dean will have the opportunity to direct the vision of an energetic and engaged faculty, staff and student population. The new Dean will enjoy the advantages of a growing endowment with strong alumni and media support. The college’s educational experience is grounded in experiential learning, giving students meaningful opportunities to apply their skills in professional, real-world settings through strong connections with media, industry, and community partners. The Dean will have the unique opportunity to lead curricular innovation during a time of rapid change in journalism, media and communication and help define the future of the profession. The college looks to an exciting future under the direction of an outstanding leader to further broaden and deepen its impact. The Position The Dean reports directly to the Executive Vice Chancellor and is the chief academic and administrative officer of the College of Journalism and Mass Communications. The Dean has the responsibility for the strategic, programmatic, financial, fundraising, and management operations that support the mission and vision of the College of Journalism and Mass Communications and its role within the university and across the state. The Dean will join a group of fellow deans and campus leaders who are collaborative, supportive and committed. The Dean works alongside campus leaders to advance the values and mission of the university, ensuring the College’s efforts are in alignment with the overall priorities and goals. The incoming Dean will: Have the opportunity to define and implement the college’s next strategic vision with the input of talented faculty, staff, students, alumni and external advisory boards; Further the development of a relevant and distinctive identity for the college; Serve as a public voice to develop the reputation of the college externally on national and international stages, within the profession and private industry; Assure the continued prominence of the faculty by prioritizing the recruiting and retention of distinguished faculty at all levels; Support and engage staff, encourage their growth, and ensure they play an active role in the College’s success and future. Cultivate academic programs that demonstrate professional relevance, impact, and sustainability, and champion the distinct, yet interconnected disciplines in the college; Work to fully realize and enact the college and university commitment to community and belonging, ensuring that all individuals and interactions matter; Seek out and continue valuable collaborations with other academic units and partners; Promote and support a strong research and creative activity agenda, including attracting external funding from federal agencies, corporations and foundations and continue to grow the College’s portfolio by expanding partnerships and pursuing new opportunities; Appreciate and foster the dual mission of research/creative activity and teaching to maintain an academic and professional focus; Assure that the college continues to serve its students with academic programs of the highest quality and effectiveness, promoting and sustaining practices for experiential learning, student success, persistence, retention, graduation and placement; Continue an upward trajectory of enrollment in the college; Engage alumni and other external supporters to advance the mission of the college; Take a leading role in attracting interested donors to support the college’s mission; and Be an engaged academic leader at the university, working collaboratively and advancing the overall mission and priorities of the campus. Minimum Required Qualifications Candidate Profile Successful candidates will have deep experience in and awareness of both the professions and academia and will bring a record of achievement that reflects a commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education, research and creative activity, and the public and professional impact of the College of Journalism and Mass Communications. Specifically, candidates should demonstrate: A Ph.D. or terminal degree in a related discipline with an outstanding record of scholarly or creative achievement and/or an outstanding record of experience in the industry, with accomplishments commensurate with the rank of full professor in the college. A track record of successful leadership in a complex academic, professional, or organizational environment, including experience leading diverse, multifaceted teams or organizations; a significant record of success as an administrator whose credibility, communication skills and collaborative management style can energize a dynamic college. A deep understanding of the academic enterprise and shared governance that clearly informs decision-making. Strong business and financial acumen, including a focus on managing resources and aligning investments with institutional priorities. The ability to cultivate academic programs, research and creative activity that demonstrate professional relevance, impact, sustainability and champion the distinct, yet interconnected disciplines in the college. A record of building effective and collaborative relationships with a broad range of constituencies both across the university and with community partners and external audiences. A strong commitment to student success, fostering access consistent with UNL’s mission as a land-grant institution. A commitment to recruiting, supporting, and retaining an accomplished faculty and staff, and cultivating an inclusive campus community. An understanding, capacity, and enthusiasm to advance development and fundraising activities. The highest level of integrity. Preferred Qualifications Additional Attributes A highly qualified candidate will also: Embody the role of advocate and champion for the College within the University setting and in the broader communities statewide and nationally. Possess and model a bold, creative, and systems-thinking approach that focuses on integrative solutions to complex problems. Take bold, courageous risks to achieve excellence. Cultivate a vision for the future by enthusiastically embracing new ideas and thinking beyond what is known today. Demonstrate comfort with and knowledge of the range of disciplines and scholarship represented through the college. Model an ethic of care and cultural consciousness for all college constituents, with a visible and accessible presence. Listen actively and model feedback to foster transparency, awareness, and understanding of decisions and outcomes throughout the college. Exhibit an authentic curiosity and inspire others. Be energized to work in a complex organization and embrace the multifaceted needs of the college and university community, including students, staff, all faculty, and external partners. Embrace the challenges and unknowns of higher education today including the enrollment landscape and bring meaningful solutions for growing the reach and impact of the college. Have navigated technological changes, adapting curricula and/or research and creative activity for emerging media technologies and evolving digital platforms, such as AI. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Yes Posted Salary How to Apply We will begin reviewing candidates immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Priority consideration will be given to those materials received by November 9, 2026. Applications should consist of a letter summarizing motivation, relevant leadership experience, and qualifications and a detailed curriculum vitae. To apply, click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty application form, and upload the following materials: Letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. The names and contact information for at least three professional references will be requested from candidates who advance to the interview stages. Questions and nominations can be sent in confidence, to: Kathy Farrell, Search Chair James Jr. and Susan Stuart Endowed Dean, College of Business University of Nebraska-Lincoln kfarrell2@unl.edu and Allison Wortmann Academic Personnel and HR Specialist University of Nebraska-Lincoln allison.wortmann@unl.edu The University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks to attract and retain a high performing and collaborative workforce. UNL is committed to providing a work environment and culture that fosters personal and professional success where every person and every interaction matters. The University is proud to be one of Nebraska’s preferred and largest employers where individuals are able to participate and contribute to their full potential. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact For questions and assistance with the application process, contact Allison Wortmann, Academic Personnel and HR Specialist, at allison.wortmann@unl.edu or by phone at (402) 472-4175. Job Category Job Category (old) Academic Administrative Job Type Full-Time Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102714": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor of Practice Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Practice Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job”, complete the faculty information form, and attach the following required documents: Cover letter addressing the applicant’s vision for technical theatre and entertainment production education in a technology-rich, interdisciplinary environment. Comprehensive CV highlighting relevant professional and teaching experience. Teaching philosophy, maximum two pages. Link to online portfolio of technical and production work, including examples such as technical drawings, process documentation, fabrication work, and concept-to-completion examples. Contact information for three professional references. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant Professor of Practice Department Johnny Carson School-Theatre & Film-1033 Requisition Number F_260112 Posting Open Date 10/07/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 12/01/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Position Overview We seek a collaborative technical leader with comprehensive expertise in scenic construction and engineering, rigging and safety, fabrication, and related production disciplines, along with experience with contemporary entertainment technologies such as Vectorworks and/or AutoCAD, automation and show-control systems, CNC fabrication, and 3D printing. The successful candidate will be committed to practice-based learning and understand how foundational craft knowledge informs and enhances technological innovation. They will bring a passion for interdisciplinary collaboration and preparing students for current and future career paths across the entertainment industry. We seek a colleague who is curious about new technologies and methodologies, comfortable working in an evolving educational and production environment, and interested in contributing to the continued development of the School’s curriculum and pedagogical approaches. The successful candidate will have experience managing complex technical operations; demonstrated project-management and leadership skills; and the ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, guest artists, and industry partners. Key Responsibilities Technical Leadership and Production Oversee the physical construction and engineering aspects of School productions, including rigging, fabrication, and safety. Develop and implement technical systems supporting both conventional and emerging production methodologies. Integrate new production technologies into existing production processes and workflows. Provide technical leadership and problem-solving across the School’s production activities. Collaborate with faculty and staff across Entertainment Design & Production, Theatre, Film, and Emerging Media Arts to develop shared technical resources and workflows. Maintain and advance professional standards for safety, fabrication, rigging, and technical production. Teaching and Mentorship Teach and mentor students in technical theatre, entertainment technology, fabrication, and evolving production methodologies. Depending upon curricular needs and the candidate’s areas of expertise, courses may include: Computer-Aided Drafting Automation and Computer-Controlled Systems Rigging Special Effects Metalworking Entertainment Engineering Advanced Materials and Fabrication Advanced Carpentry CNC and Dimensional Printing Technologies The successful candidate will mentor students through hands-on, practice-based learning and help them connect foundational construction and fabrication skills with contemporary entertainment technologies. Curriculum and Interdisciplinary Collaboration Develop course work within the curricular structure that connects traditional craft, fabrication, engineering, and emerging production technologies. Foster interdisciplinary learning opportunities across theatre, film, and emerging media. Explore new technologies, methodologies, and teaching approaches as entertainment production continues to evolve. Contribute, as appropriate, to online and digitally supported curriculum development. Facilities and Technical Resources Contribute to the strategic development of technical facilities supporting the School’s expanding curricular and production needs. Help oversee scene shops, fabrication spaces, prop and storage areas, and associated making and production facilities. Ensure that facilities and technical practices meet current safety standards while supporting innovative production practices. Participate in planning for equipment, technologies, and infrastructure supporting Entertainment Design & Production and interdisciplinary production. Professional and Industry Engagement Maintain active engagement with current practices and emerging technologies within the entertainment industry. Help develop student connections to internships, apprenticeships, professional opportunities, and industry partners. Represent the School through appropriate professional organizations, conferences, and industry engagement. Contribute to conversations about the changing nature of technical production and entertainment education. Minimum Required Qualifications BFA in Technical Theatre or a related field with significant professional experience in lieu of a terminal degree. Minimum two years of professional experience in technical direction or related production work for live entertainment. Demonstrated expertise in traditional theatrical craft, construction, fabrication, and contemporary entertainment technology. One year of collegiate teaching experience or equivalent professional training, mentorship, or instructional experience. Demonstrated project-management and leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications MFA in Technical Theatre or a related field. Five or more years of professional experience in technical direction or related entertainment production. Two or more years of teaching experience in higher education. Experience with emerging technologies such as automation, virtual production, motion capture, real-time systems, interactive media, or advanced digital fabrication. Experience in film production, themed entertainment, immersive experiences, live events, or other forms of mediated entertainment. Professional connections across entertainment technology, themed entertainment, live performance, film, or related industries. Experience developing curriculum, including online or digitally supported modalities. Professional certifications in relevant software, safety practices, rigging, fabrication, or technical systems. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job”, complete the faculty information form, and attach the following required documents: Cover letter addressing the applicant’s vision for technical theatre and entertainment production education in a technology-rich, interdisciplinary environment. Comprehensive CV highlighting relevant professional and teaching experience. Teaching philosophy, maximum two pages. Link to online portfolio of technical and production work, including examples such as technical drawings, process documentation, fabrication work, and concept-to-completion examples. Contact information for three professional references. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Hank Stratton, hstratton2@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Non-Tenure Leading Job Type Full-Time Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/16/2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Online Portfolio Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102713": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Elementary Mathematics Education",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor - Elementary Mathematics Education Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor - Elementary Mathematics Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty application, and attach the following required documents: Letter of application outlining your qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references who will be contacted and/or asked to provide letters of recommendation. Teaching statement. Research statement. Two examples of scholarly work. Transcripts or unofficial copies of transcripts from the doctoral program (official copies of transcripts will be required at time of offer). Please combine items 4, 5, 6, and 7 into a single document and attach as \"Other Document.\" For additional questions, please contact Dr. Amanda Henson, Search Committee Chair, at amanda.thomas@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant Professor - Elementary Mathematics Education Department Teaching, Learning & Teacher Ed-1045 Requisition Number F_260103 Posting Open Date 10/07/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Teaching, Learning and Teacher Education ( https://cehs.unl.edu/tlte ) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln invites applications for a tenure-line Assistant Professor of Elementary Mathematics Education who can help prepare effective educators, collaborate with department colleagues, mathematics and STEM content specialists, and classroom teachers, as well as attract increased national interest and funding to nationally visible programs in mathematics education at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln. Our new colleague will be joining a dynamic and committed community of scholars in the department and a collaborative faculty group in elementary education. The K-6 teacher preparation program graduates approximately 150 teacher candidates annually and benefits from long-standing and unique partnerships with the Department of Mathematics in the College of Arts and Sciences and the Center for Science, Mathematics and Computer Education. We anticipate expanding our faculty in elementary, secondary, and mathematics education not only to prepare students for initial teacher certification, but also to provide professional learning in graduate education and expand opportunities for funded research and scholarship. Position Responsibilities Teach Elementary Mathematics methods coursework as part of a collaborative undergraduate STEM Block of courses. Teach graduate courses in K-12 Mathematics Education and other areas of expertise. Advise and mentor master’s and doctoral students. Conduct a scholarly program of research appropriate to rank. Engage actively in collaboration and development within and across content areas, programs, departments, and colleges. Provide outreach to schools, other educational institutions, and communities. UNL is the University of Nebraska system’s flagship university and a member of the Big 10 Academic Alliance. TLTE is recognized across UNL for distinguished teaching, strong collaborations with exceptional partner schools, and it has a reputation for scholarship that embraces diverse research methodologies. The candidates who fill these positions will teach and advise undergraduate and graduate students in mathematics education. TLTE seeks a colleague who possesses the understanding, commitment, and ability to contribute collaboratively to robust elementary (and secondary education) programs and mathematics education in the context of continuing demographic change in the state and nation. The College of Education and Human Sciences strives to be a vibrant, welcoming, and caring community driven by our mission to enhance the lives of individuals, families, schools, and communities, and strengthening the relationships among them. At the University of Nebraska, we strive for excellence in all that we do. True excellence requires that every individual is able to work and learn in an atmosphere of respect, dignity, and acceptance. Our commitment to excellence requires each of us to continuously ensure our interactions be respectful, protect free speech, and inspire academic freedom. Minimum Required Qualifications Doctorate in mathematics education, curriculum and instruction, teacher education, or a related field. ABD candidates will be considered, but a doctoral degree must be completed before the position start date. A minimum of two (2) years of elementary or secondary teaching experience. Preparation to teach college-level mathematics education courses. A clear research agenda anchored elementary mathematics education and/or teacher education that is commensurate with expectations of a research-intensive institution. Evidence of professional and institutional service. Demonstrated commitment to access and equity in teaching and scholarship. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated mentoring and advising abilities. Experience teaching at the college level. Experience teaching courses in a variety of formats (e.g., in person, online, hybrid, site-based). Participation in funded projects (particularly in seeking and/or securing external funding). Demonstrated success working with students from diverse cultures and backgrounds. Experience in interdisciplinary program/course development. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job,” complete the faculty application, and attach the following required documents: Letter of application outlining your qualifications for the position. Curriculum vitae. Contact information for three professional references who will be contacted and/or asked to provide letters of recommendation. Teaching statement. Research statement. Two examples of scholarly work. Transcripts or unofficial copies of transcripts from the doctoral program (official copies of transcripts will be required at time of offer). Please combine items 4, 5, 6, and 7 into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” For additional questions, please contact Dr. Amanda Henson, Search Committee Chair, at amanda.thomas@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Dr. Amanda Henson Search Committee Chair amanda.thomas@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date August 16, 2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102693": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Cardiometabolic Disease",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Postdoctoral Research Associate - Cardiometabolic Disease Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Postdoctoral Research Associate - Cardiometabolic Disease Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A letter of interest that describes your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments where every person and every interaction matters. See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three (3) professional references. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Postdoctoral Research Associate - Cardiometabolic Disease Department Biochemistry-0831 Requisition Number F_260113 Posting Open Date 10/07/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Biochemistry at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources ( IANR ) is seeking applications for a highly motivated and enthusiastic post-doctoral research associate. Located in Lincoln, Nebraska, this 12-month (calendar year), 100% research, special appointment will: Perform in-depth literature searches to inform research strategies and develop protocols. Design and execute mechanistic experiments in vascular and inflammatory biology. Perform in vivo studies using murine models such as atherosclerosis, fatty liver, and acute lung injury. Conduct cell and organoid culture. Analyze molecular, physiological, and histological data and interpret results. Perform advanced bioinformatics analysis, employing cutting-edge bioinformatics tools. Help train and mentor students, including undergraduate students, rotating students, and Ph.D. students. Prepare manuscripts, abstracts, and grant applications. Present findings at national scientific meetings. Assist lab management and take lab responsibilities, such as ordering and organizing lab supplies. In addition to the above-described duties, the individual will be expected to accept committee assignments, reporting responsibilities, and other special ad hoc assignments as requested at the administrative unit, college/division, institute, and/or university level. Recognizing that collaboration and participation in teams enhances creativity, innovation, impact, and a sense of belonging, the Institute of Agriculture and Natural Resources ( IANR ) and the Department of Biochemistry are committed to creating learning, research, and Extension programming environments where the unique contributions of each individual are acknowledged and valued. At IANR ,we see every person and every interaction as important to our collective wellbeing and our ability to deliver on our mission. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in physiology, biochemistry, biomedical sciences, or a related field. Strong experience in biochemical and molecular biology techniques, tissue processing and immunostaining, and small animal studies. Must have at least one first-author peer-reviewed publication from the last two years. Preferred Qualifications Interest in learning advanced bioinformatic analysis such as analyzing single-cell RNA -seq data. Highly motivated for research independence and career advancement. Demonstrated excellent verbal and written communication skills, and interpersonal skills. Experiences in cell culture of primary endothelial cells, hepatocytes, and hepatic stellate cells, and organoid culture. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A letter of interest that describes your experience working in teams or groups and your anticipated contributions to creating environments where every person and every interaction matters. See https://go.unl.edu/ianrguide for guidance in writing this statement. Your curriculum vitae. Contact information for three (3) professional references. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Marci Sturek msturek2@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Post Docs & Other Academic Job Type 12 Month (Faculty Only) Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? Yes If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102674": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Computer Engineering",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant/Associate Professor - Computer Engineering Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor - Computer Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply to this job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A cover letter. CV. A research statement; a statement describing your teaching and mentoring practices; and a statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the College of Engineering Complete Engineer ® Program ( engineering.unl.edu/complete-engineer ). Combine into a single document and attach as \"Other Document.\" List of three references. After review of applications begins, those with any missing required statements may not be given full consideration. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor - Computer Engineering Department Electrical & Computer Engineering-1063 Requisition Number F_260100 Posting Open Date 09/28/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 12/04/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at UNL is seeking applicants for a tenure-line position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor with a focus in computer engineering systems, computer architecture, or networking, including connections to systems engineering. The person hired into this position is expected to develop a nationally recognized research program and contribute to academic programs in computer engineering, with opportunities to support interdisciplinary systems engineering research and education. Research and educational activities may include: Developing an externally funded research program in computer engineering systems, computer architecture, or networking. Developing and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in these areas to prepare students for careers in industry, research, and academia. Mentoring undergraduate and graduate students and advancing collaborative research, capstone projects, and industry partnerships. The position will be based on the Scott Campus in Omaha, NE, and housed in the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, with opportunities to support teaching and research on UNL’s City Campus in Lincoln. This location will facilitate collaboration with faculty across Nebraska Engineering, the University of Nebraska at Omaha, and relevant industry and government partners. Candidates are expected to have an outstanding publication record, a history of funded research, and a strong national/international reputation in the area of computer and system engineering and related topics. Preference will be given to candidates with experience building higher education degree programs. As part of this initiative, the Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering ( https://ece.unl.edu ) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant/Associate Professor level that will provide a nucleus for further hiring in this technical area. The Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering consists of approximately 35 tenured/tenure-track faculty, 400 undergraduate students, and 120 graduate students co-located in two cities, Lincoln and Omaha, Nebraska. An outstanding infrastructure exists for conducting research, including central facilities housing state-of-the-art instrumentation and computing, including the Holland Computing Center ( https://hcc.unl.edu ). Opportunities for collaborations across the University of Nebraska include the University of Nebraska Medical Center; the University of Nebraska-Omaha College of Information Science & Technology; the Nebraska Center for Energy Sciences Research; the Center for Brain, Biology, and Behavior; the Nebraska Athletic Performance Laboratory; the Midwest Roadside Safety Facility; Innovation Campus; and other state- and federally-funded research centers and programs. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in electrical engineering, computer engineering, or a closely aligned area. Demonstrated experience in computer engineering teaching and research. The ability to think broadly and develop research and programmatic activities. The understanding of how to build productive relationships with faculty, students, administrative leaders, and external partners across various disciplines and organizational units. Preferred Qualifications Possess credentials and a distinguished scholarly record that qualifies the applicant for a tenured faculty position in the electrical and computer engineering department. Passion for promoting and developing strong partnerships with industry, other universities, government agencies such as STRATCOM , and other partners. Experience with mentoring undergraduate students. Work Location (City, State) Omaha, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply to this job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A cover letter. CV. A research statement; a statement describing your teaching and mentoring practices; and a statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the College of Engineering Complete Engineer ® Program ( engineering.unl.edu/complete-engineer ). Combine into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” List of three references. After review of applications begins, those with any missing required statements may not be given full consideration. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Hamid Sharif, Professor and Search Chair hamidsharif@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/16/2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102673": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following required documents: Letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. Research statement. Teaching statement. Up to three publications. List of three professional references. The statements and publications will need to be combined into a single document and attached as \"Other Document.\" Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant Professor Department Psychology-1094 Requisition Number F_260099 Posting Open Date 10/05/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 11/06/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Psychology Department at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln is recruiting a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Addiction Science who studies antecedents, processes, and/or consequences of substance use and/or misuse. Potential areas of interest include but are not limited to developmental trajectories and/or aging processes; biological and neurobehavioral mechanisms, including human or animal models; social and interpersonal processes; addiction-related cognition and decision-making; risk and resilience factors such as trauma, stress, or comorbidity with mental health disorders; and addiction-related prevention, treatment, policy, and laws. Experience with advanced quantitative approaches is welcome but not required for the position. Responsibilities include maintaining an active research program, including the pursuit of external funding, and teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in addiction and substance use. Given that addiction and substance use are integral to a number of other disciplines, the successful candidate could be a valuable contributor to multidisciplinary research efforts involving multiple units on campus (e.g., Center for Brain, Biology & Behavior; Rural Drug Addiction Research Center; Minority Health Disparities Initiative; Nebraska Athletic Performance Lab; Center for Research on Children, Youth, Families, and Schools; Center on Children, Families, and the Law; the College of Education and Human Sciences; the Law School). The Department of Psychology values a collegial and supportive working environment in which a range of experiences and perspectives strengthens research and teaching, and we welcome applicants who will contribute to that environment. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in psychology or a related field is required by the start date. Research experience in addiction science and/or substance use. A successful history of scholarly publications in peer-reviewed journals. Research interests that connect to the Rural Drug Use Addiction Research Center. Teaching experience in psychology or related areas. Evidence of the ability to work effectively with students from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Preferred Qualifications Relevant experience post-Ph.D. Experience with advanced quantitative approaches. Research interests that complement current faculty expertise (e.g., cognitive psychology, clinical psychology, developmental psychology, law-psychology, neuroscience, or social psychology). A successful history of external and/or internal funding. Evidence of mentoring students in a research setting. Teaching experience in the field of addiction science or substance use. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following required documents: Letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. Research statement. Teaching statement. Up to three publications. List of three professional references. The statements and publications will need to be combined into a single document and attached as “Other Document.” For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Tierney Lorenz tierney.lorenz@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/01/2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102646": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Advanced Manufacturing",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor - Advanced Manufacturing Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor - Advanced Manufacturing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Research statement. Teaching statement. A statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the COE Complete Engineer® Program . A list of three to five professional references with full names and contact information. Please combine the statements (items 3, 4, and 5) into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant Professor - Advanced Manufacturing Department Mechanical & Materials Engineering-1067 Requisition Number F_260109 Posting Open Date 10/02/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 01/04/2027 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Mechanical & Materials Engineering ( https://engineering.unl.edu/mme ) at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. The successful candidate is expected to develop an internationally recognized research program in advanced manufacturing and support a new undergraduate degree program in industrial engineering. We seek innovative and inspirational scholars with a commitment to excellence in teaching, research, service, and engagement. The Department of Mechanical & Materials Engineering ( MME ) consists of approximately 30 tenured/tenure-track faculty, over 900 undergraduate students, and 100 graduate students. Recent investments in the College of Engineering include a new ~$80M research building and a new $120M teaching and learning building. UNL supports an outstanding system of central facilities housing state-of-the-art instrumentation and computation capabilities within the Nebraska Center for Materials and Nanoscience ( ncmn.unl.edu ), the Nebraska Nanoengineering Research Core Facility ( engineering.unl.edu/nercf ), Nebraska Engineering Additive Technologies (neatlabs.unl.edu), and the Holland Computing Center ( hcc.unl.edu ). Opportunities for collaborations across the University of Nebraska include the University of Nebraska Medical Center, the Nebraska Center for Energy Sciences Research, the National Strategic Research Institute ( NSRI ), the Nebraska Center for Materials and Nanoscience, the Center for Electro-Optics and Functionalized Surfaces, the Center for Brain, Biology, and Behavior, the Nebraska Athletic Performance Laboratory, the Midwest Roadside Safety Facility, Innovation Campus, and other state- and federally-funded research centers and programs. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. or equivalent in industrial engineering, mechanical engineering, or a closely related field. Record of strong scholarly achievement. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate and graduate education. Potential to establish a strong externally funded research program Expertise to contribute to undergraduate and graduate degree programs, with particular focus on strengthening curriculum related to industrial engineering. Preferred Qualifications Research areas of interest relate to the broad area of intelligent/advanced manufacturing, including but not limited to digital manufacturing and digital twins; sensing, process control, robotics and automation, qualification, and optimization; and supply-chain resilience and sustainability. AI/ML-enabled approaches in manufacturing research and education are of particular interest. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Research statement. Teaching statement. A statement of how your combined professional and academic experiences have equipped you to make a valuable contribution to the COE Complete Engineer® Program . A list of three to five professional references with full names and contact information. Please combine the statements (items 3, 4, and 5) into a single document and attach as “Other Document.” For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Jung Yul Lim, Professor and Search Committee Chair jlim4@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/16/2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
