    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102538": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: Letter of interest. A detailed resume or CV that includes information on education, experience, research publications/working papers, and teaching experience, if applicable (including title and levels of courses taught and summary of teaching evaluations). A list of three references with complete contact information. One published or working research paper (optional). Additional supporting material that the candidate may want to submit (optional). Combine the research paper and supporting materials (items 4 and 5) into a single document and upload as \"Other Document.\" The application must be complete before it can be evaluated. For questions about the application process, please email Michelle Jacobs ( mjacobs1@unl.edu ). For questions about the position, email the chair of the search committee, Dr. Sajeesh Sajeesh ( ssajeesh2@unl.edu ). Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See: Notice of Nondiscrimination Working Title Assistant Professor Department Marketing-1028 Requisition Number F_260097 Posting Open Date 09/28/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/30/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work Position Summary The College of Business at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln seeks applicants for a tenure-track, Assistant Professor level position starting Fall 2027. Applicants should demonstrate the ability and qualifications commensurate with the rank of Assistant Professor. Upon hiring, they are also expected to show successful and ongoing involvement in the Department and the College’s research, service, and teaching (undergraduate and graduate programs). About the Department of Marketing The Department of Marketing ( https://business.unl.edu/marketing/ ) has 15 faculty members. It provides a very collegial environment for research and teaching. The Agribusiness Program and the Center for Sales Excellence are also housed in the department, offering resources and opportunities for collaboration with industry partners. About the College of Business The College of Business drives discovery, creates opportunity, and empowers its record-breaking 4,534 students to lead the future of business. Programs include 12 undergraduate majors and numerous graduate programs, including our highly-ranked online MBA , three online master of science degrees, and two Ph.D. programs. Established in 1913, it is the only doctorate granting business college in Nebraska. Howard L. Hawks Hall, located at 14th and Vine Streets, has been home to the college since 2017. Hawks Hall features interactive learning in state-of-the-art classrooms, cutting-edge technology and one-stop student support services, including free one-on-one tutoring and coaching. For more information, visit https://business.unl.edu/ . About the University of Nebraska–Lincoln We are proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and certified as a Family Friendly Workplace. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. About Lincoln, Nebraska Home to the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, the city of Lincoln consistently ranks one of the happiest cities in America and highest for livability thanks to a low cost of living, great schools and friendly, community-minded residents. Set amidst a big sky and open landscape, the state’s capital city is simple to navigate with a nationally noted low crime rate, a wide range of housing choices and a reliable public transit system. As one of the fastest growing metro areas in the Midwest, Lincoln boasts a growing technology sector, more parkland per capita than all but a few U.S. cities, an extensive bike trail network, and numerous options for recreational and personal interest activities. It’s easy to feel at home here. Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in marketing or a related discipline from an AACSB or equivalent accredited School or College of Business at the time of the appointment. Demonstrated ability to conduct high-quality research aimed at top-tier marketing journals. Research in the domain of managerial marketing (e.g., marketing strategy, B2B, sales). Ability to teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Experience and credentials commensurate with the rank of Assistant Professor. Preferred Qualifications Published manuscripts or invited revisions in top-tier marketing journals. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: Letter of interest. A detailed resume or CV that includes information on education, experience, research publications/working papers, and teaching experience, if applicable (including title and levels of courses taught and summary of teaching evaluations). A list of three references with complete contact information. One published or working research paper (optional). Additional supporting material that the candidate may want to submit (optional). Combine the research paper and supporting materials (items 4 and 5) into a single document and upload as “Other Document.” The application must be complete before it can be evaluated. For questions about the application process, please email Michelle Jacobs ( mjacobs1@unl.edu ). For questions about the position, email the chair of the search committee, Dr. Sajeesh Sajeesh ( ssajeesh2@unl.edu ). For questions or accommodations related to this position contact For questions about the application process, please email Michelle Jacobs ( mjacobs1@unl.edu ). For questions about the position, please email the chair of the search committee, Dr. Sajeesh Sajeesh ( ssajeesh2@unl.edu ). Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Other Document Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102488": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A letter of interest that addresses your qualifications and interest in the position. A curriculum vitae. A list of three references with contact information. One document containing: i) a sample of publications or working papers, and ii) evidence of teaching experience and ability. Attach as “Other Document.” All four documents are required for a complete file. Only complete files will be reviewed. Interested candidates may reach out to the chair of the search, Dr. Rob Campbell (rob.campbell@unl.edu) with any questions. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See <a href=“https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/”>Notice of Nondiscrimination</a>. Working Title Assistant Professor Department Management-1027 Requisition Number F_260094 Posting Open Date 09/24/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/26/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Management in the College of Business at the University of Nebraska-Lincoln ( UNL ) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Strategic Management at the rank of Assistant Professor, with an expected start date of August 2027. We seek colleagues who can contribute to the College’s research mission and degree programs at the undergraduate, MBA , and Ph.D. levels, and other areas as appropriate. We seek individuals who are interested in being active members of a rich and collegial academic community. Given UNL’s status as a Big Ten institution, salary, benefits, and research support are competitive. About the Department The Department of Management ( https://business.unl.edu/management/ ) currently includes 25 total faculty members, including 14 tenured/tenure-track faculty, and provides a collegial environment for research and teaching. Our faculty members regularly publish in top-tier management journals and are awarded for their research and teaching accomplishments. Indeed, according to the TAMUGA rankings of Management Department productivity, the department is ranked 29th on a per faculty basis for the 2021-2025 time period. We enjoy sharing our research in progress within the department to solicit ideas and feedback and regularly invite visiting faculty to do the same. The Center for Entrepreneurship, International Business program, and the Clifton Strengths Institute are affiliated with the Department of Management and administered by Management faculty. About the College of Business The College of Business drives discovery, creates opportunity, and empowers its record-breaking 4,534 students to lead the future of business. Programs include 12 undergraduate majors and numerous graduate programs, including our highly-ranked online MBA , three online master of science degrees, and two Ph.D. programs. Established in 1913, it is the only doctorate granting business college in Nebraska. Howard L. Hawks Hall, located at 14th and Vine Streets, has been home to the college since 2017. Hawks Hall features interactive learning in state-of-the-art classrooms, cutting-edge technology, and one-stop student support services, including free one-on-one tutoring and coaching. For more information, visit https://business.unl.edu . About the University of Nebraska–Lincoln We are proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and certified as a Family Friendly Workplace. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. About Lincoln, Nebraska Home to the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, the city of Lincoln consistently ranks one of the happiest cities in America and highest for livability thanks to a low cost of living, great schools, and friendly, community-minded residents. Set amidst a big sky and open landscape, the state’s capital city is simple to navigate with a nationally noted low crime rate, a wide range of housing choices, and a reliable public transit system. As one of the fastest growing metro areas in the Midwest, Lincoln boasts a growing technology sector, more parkland per capita than all but a few U.S. cities, an extensive bike trail network, and numerous options for recreational and personal interest activities. It’s easy to feel at home here. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Strategic Management or a closely related field. Advanced ABD candidates will be considered; the degree must be conferred at the time of the appointment start date. Applicants must demonstrate a research program relevant to Strategic Management and a history of targeting top-tier management-related journals. Candidates for this position must also have teaching experience and an interest in teaching at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching Strategic Management at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Ability and interest to teach Entrepreneurship courses. Candidates who can contribute to teaching across both areas are especially encouraged . Demonstrated ability to publish in top-tier management journals. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A letter of interest that addresses your qualifications and interest in the position. A curriculum vitae. A list of three references with contact information. One document containing: i) a sample of publications or working papers, and ii) evidence of teaching experience and ability. Attach as “Other Document.” All four documents are required for a complete file. Only complete files will be reviewed. Interested candidates may reach out to the chair of the search, Dr. Rob Campbell (rob.campbell@unl.edu) with any questions. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact If you have questions about this position, please email Dr. Rob Campbell at rob.campbell@unl.edu . For specific questions about the application process, please email Melissa Lewis at melissa.lewis@unl.edu . Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102394": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A letter of interest that addresses your qualifications and interest in the position. A curriculum vitae. A list of three references with contact information. One document containing: i) a sample of publications or working papers, and ii) evidence of teaching experience and ability. Attach as \"Other Document.\" All four documents are required for a complete file. Only complete files will be reviewed. Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Assistant Professor Department School of Accountancy-1029 Requisition Number F_260091 Posting Open Date 09/21/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/26/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The School of Accountancy invites applications for a tenure-track appointment at the Assistant Professor rank beginning August 2027. All areas of teaching and research interest will be considered; however, our primary teaching need is in taxation. Qualified candidates must hold a Ph.D. in accounting or a related field from an AACSB accredited institution by the time of appointment. The successful candidate will be expected to publish high-quality research in leading accounting or closely related discipline journals and contribute to the School’s teaching mission. We are particularly interested in individuals who are strong organizational citizens and are interested in being active members of a rich academic community. Salary, benefits, and research support are competitive. About the School of Accountancy The School of Accountancy ( https://business.unl.edu/academic-programs/departments/accounting/ ) has 11 tenured or tenure-track faculty and 6 Professors of Practice. It provides a very collegial environment for research and teaching. About the College of Business The College of Business drives discovery, creates opportunity and empowers its record-breaking 4,534 students to lead the future of business. Programs include 12 undergraduate majors and numerous graduate programs, including our on campus Masters of Professional Accountancy program, highly-ranked online MBA , three online master of science degrees, and two Ph.D. programs. Established in 1913, it is the only doctorate granting business college in Nebraska. Howard L. Hawks Hall, located at 14th and Vine Streets, has been home of the college since 2017. Hawks Hall features interactive learning in state-of-the-art classrooms, cutting-edge technology and one-stop student support services, including free one-on-one tutoring and coaching. For more information, visit https://business.unl.edu About the University of Nebraska–Lincoln We are proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer and certified as a Family Friendly Workplace. We are known for our welcoming, supportive environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace; it’s a place to build your career and make a meaningful impact in Nebraska. About Lincoln, Nebraska Home to the University of Nebraska–Lincoln, the city of Lincoln consistently ranks one of the happiest cities in America and highest for livability thanks to a low cost of living, great schools and friendly, community-minded residents. Set amidst a big sky and open landscape, the state’s capital city is simple to navigate with a nationally noted low crime rate, a wide range of housing choices, and a reliable public transit system. As one of the fastest growing metro areas in the Midwest, Lincoln boasts a growing technology sector, more parkland per capita than all but a few U.S. cities, an extensive bike trail network, and numerous options for recreational and personal interest activities. It’s easy to feel at home here. For specific questions about the position, please email Search Committee Chair Tom Kubick at tkubick@unl.edu . The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Ph.D. in accounting or a related field from an AACSB accredited institution by the time of appointment. Preferred Qualifications All areas of teaching and research interest will be considered; however, our primary teaching need is in taxation. We are particularly interested in individuals who are strong organizational citizens and are interested in being active members of a rich academic community. The successful candidate will be expected to publish high-quality research in leading accounting or closely related discipline journals and contribute to the School’s teaching mission. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: A letter of interest that addresses your qualifications and interest in the position. A curriculum vitae. A list of three references with contact information. One document containing: i) a sample of publications or working papers, and ii) evidence of teaching experience and ability. Attach as “Other Document.” All four documents are required for a complete file. Only complete files will be reviewed. For questions or accommodations related to this position contact For specific questions about the position, please email Search Committee Chair Tom Kubick at tkubick@unl.edu. Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102360": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Audiology",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant/Associate Professor - Audiology Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate Professor - Audiology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Upload the following documents: Letter of interest that includes research and teaching statements describing your experiences, accomplishments, philosophy, and future goals in each area. Curriculum vitae. A statement of up to one page that describes your anticipated contributions to creating inclusive environments in which every person and every interaction matters. Attach as \"Other Document.\" Contact information for three professional references who may be asked to provide recommendations by phone or by letter. For additional questions, please contact Search Committee Chair Dr. Emily Wakefield at emily.wakefield@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor - Audiology Department Special Ed & Communic Disorders-1049 Requisition Number F_260092 Posting Open Date 09/18/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/21/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The Department of Special Education and Communication Disorders at the University of Nebraska–Lincoln ( UNL ) is seeking applications for a tenure-leading Assistant or Associate Professor in Audiology. This 9-month (academic year) appointment will contribute to the department’s teaching and research missions, with an emphasis on developing a nationally and internationally recognized research program in audiology. This position will be located in Lincoln, Nebraska, with a projected start date of August 16, 2027. The Department of Special Education and Communication Disorders at UNL is housed in a state-of-the-art facility in a newly expanded and renovated building. We have access to teaching and research equipment and resources that can help you launch a successful career. You will teach alongside our expert faculty in our spiral curriculum, where we integrate the expertise of our clinical and research faculty to create an environment where students are coached to make connections between research and practice. Our proximity to and collaborations with Boys Town National Research Hospital, Madonna Rehabilitation Hospital, UNL’s Center for Brain, Biology, and Behavior (CB3), and the University of Nebraska Medical Center may provide opportunities for you to build your program of research. We are excited to welcome a new colleague at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor with expertise in audiology to join our collaborative and supportive faculty. We are especially interested in candidates whose work focuses on hearing and balance sciences, amplification and hearing aids, vestibular assessment and management, cognition and aging, or pediatric audiology. At the same time, we encourage applicants from a wide range of research areas who share our commitment to advancing knowledge and improving the lives of individuals with hearing and balance needs. RESPONSIBILITIES Build a collaborative research program that contributes to the advancement of audiology and has the potential to attract external support; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in areas of expertise; mentor and guide student research; and engage in professional service within the department, college, university, and broader community. MORE ABOUT US The Department of Special Education and Communication Disorders ( https://cehs.unl.edu/secd ) houses graduate programs in Audiology, Speech Language Pathology, and Special Education. SECD’s Audiology program is ranked among the top 20 audiology programs in the U.S. Faculty conduct cutting-edge research in global hearing health, communication access, hearing aids, cochlear implants, and neuroimaging. Our research thrives through interprofessional and interdepartmental collaboration, bringing together expertise from speech-language pathology, special education, engineering, athletics, psychology, and beyond. The College of Education and Human Sciences strives to be a vibrant, welcoming, and caring community driven by our mission to enhance the lives of individuals, families, schools, and communities, and strengthening the relationships among them. At the University of Nebraska-Lincoln, we’re proud to be consistently recognized by Forbes as a top employer, known for our welcoming and supportive work environment, commitment to professional growth, and outstanding benefits. UNL isn’t just a workplace, it’s a place to build your career and make a real impact in Nebraska. Lincoln, Nebraska, is a vibrant and welcoming city of over 300,000 people that blends the cultural richness of a Big Ten university community with the affordability and ease of Midwestern living. The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications Earned research doctorate (Ph.D.) in Audiology, Hearing Science, Speech Science, Neuroscience, or a closely related field. Demonstrated potential for excellence in research publications, grant activity, or research trajectory. Evidence of effective teaching or training at the undergraduate or graduate level. Preferred Qualifications Strong record or promise of obtaining external funding. Experience in both basic and applied audiology research. Clinical audiology experience and the ability to integrate clinical practice with teaching and research. Expertise in one or more of the interest areas: hearing and balance sciences, amplification and hearing aids, vestibular assessment and management, cognition and aging, or pediatric audiology. Existing collaborations with clinical or medical research centers. Skills or experience in mentoring graduate students. Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Upload the following documents: Letter of interest that includes research and teaching statements describing your experiences, accomplishments, philosophy, and future goals in each area. Curriculum vitae. A statement of up to one page that describes your anticipated contributions to creating inclusive environments in which every person and every interaction matters. Attach as “Other Document.” Contact information for three professional references who may be asked to provide recommendations by phone or by letter. For additional questions, please contact Search Committee Chair Dr. Emily Wakefield at emily.wakefield@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Dr. Emily Wakefield Search Committee Chair Email: emily.wakefield@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date 08/16/2027 Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Other Document Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://employment.unl.edu/postings/102190": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "University of Nebraska-Lincoln | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Skip to Main Content University of Nebraska-Lincoln Employment Website Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: 1. A letter of interest. 2. Curriculum vitae. 3. Names and contact information for three professional references. For questions about the application process, please contact Eric Berger, University of Nebraska College of Law, Lincoln, NE 68583-0902, or send an email to lawappointments@unl.edu . Position Information Position Information EEO Statement Working Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Department College of Law-0899 Requisition Number F_260085 Posting Open Date 09/04/2026 Application Review Date: (To ensure consideration, please submit all application materials before review date) 10/09/2026 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Description of Work The University of Nebraska College of Law invites applications for entry-level and lateral candidates for multiple tenure-track or tenured faculty positions, depending on the candidate’s experience. The primary course needs are First-Year Property and Federal Income Tax. Other course needs include Torts, Corporate Tax, Partnership Tax, Tax-related seminar, Professional Responsibility, Privacy Law, Constitutional Law, Cyber Security Law, Employee Benefits, Real Estate Transactions, Environmental Law, Administrative Law, Natural Resources Law, and Wills and Trusts. General information about the Law College is available at https://law.unl.edu/ . The University of Nebraska does not discriminate based on race, color, ethnicity, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, and/or political affiliation in its programs, activities, or employment. See https://equity.unl.edu/notice-nondiscrimination/ . Minimum Required Qualifications J.D. Degree or equivalent. Superior academic record. Demonstrated interest in relevant substantive areas. The title of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor will be based on the successful candidate’s qualifications. Preferred Qualifications Work Location (City, State) Lincoln, NE Pre-Placement Driving Record Review Required Criminal History Background Check Required No Posted Salary How to Apply Click “Apply for this Job” and complete the faculty information form. Attach the following documents: 1. A letter of interest. 2. Curriculum vitae. 3. Names and contact information for three professional references. For questions about the application process, please contact Eric Berger, University of Nebraska College of Law, Lincoln, NE 68583-0902, or send an email to lawappointments@unl.edu . For questions or accommodations related to this position contact Eric Berger lawappointments@unl.edu Job Category Job Category (old) Faculty Tenure/Tenure Leading Job Type 9 Month Position funded by grant or other form of temporary funding? No If Temporary, indicate end date Planned Hire Date Appointment End Date Organizational Location Default Location Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Required Documents Required Documents Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae List of References Optional Documents Connect with #UNL UNLincoln on Facebook @UNLincoln on Twitter UNL on YouTube @unlincoln on Instagram University of Nebraska–Lincoln on LinkedIn unlincoln on Pinterest UNLincoln on Snapchat unlincoln on Spotify Campus Links Directory Employment Events Libraries Maps Office of the Chancellor Nebraska Today Policies Emergency Planning and Preparedness Institutional Equity and Compliance Notice of Nondiscrimination Privacy Policy Student Information Disclosures TIPS Incident Reporting University of Nebraska–Lincoln About the Big Ten Conference © 2017 University of Nebraska–Lincoln · 402-472-7211 University of Nebraska System To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
